**Use `getSecureInvoice` for the normal invoice routes.**

The default app sends authenticated requests for the invoice API, assistant tool, and export through `getInvoice`. The changed query accepts any existing invoice ID. A Cedar user can therefore request `INV-2002` and receive Maple's invoice. Keep `getInvoice` only for the explicit insecure lab variant.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-    const invoice = getInvoice(store.db, req.actor, req.params.id);
+    const invoice = getSecureInvoice(store.db, req.actor, req.params.id);
...
-    const invoice = getInvoice(store.db, req.actor, String(req.body?.invoiceId || ''));
+    const invoice = getSecureInvoice(store.db, req.actor, String(req.body?.invoiceId || ''));
...
-    const invoice = getInvoice(store.db, req.actor, req.params.id);
+    const invoice = getSecureInvoice(store.db, req.actor, req.params.id);
```

</details>

Validate all three routes by signing in as Cedar and requesting `INV-2002`; each route must return `404`.
